{"school":{"dbn":"11X181","name":"I.S. 181 Pablo Casals","boro":"Bronx","district":"11","district_label":"District 11","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":489,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"800 BAYCHESTER AVENUE, BRONX, NY 10475","phone":"718-892-5270","website":"www.ms181info.weebly.com","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/70648","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"Middle School 181 is focused on developing the whole child through a balance of academic and enrichment opportunities in the arts (see activities). Middle School 181 offers two outstanding programs. Our Community Service program is deeply embedded in rigorous curriculum and the fundamental ideologies of 21st Century Learning. Engaging activities in which investigating, problem solving and students at the center of learning are evident in all courses at Middle School 181. All students are provided with their own device and participate in a two-year, four course STEAM program, in which they cycle through two unique courses each year. These courses journey students through hands-on, project-based learning experiences using technology and afford students opportunities to apply computer coding skills to program flying drones, build objects using 3D printing and create working robots. Additionally, all students participate in a special 3-year Mathematics and Science program that culminates with all grade 8 students being offered the opportunity to participate in the Algebra 1 and Living Environment course.  Our students in the honors program also participate in the U.S. History course. Each of these accelerated courses culminate with students taking Regents exams and earning high school credit in their eighth grade year. Honors students also participate in the STEAM experiences listed above. Middle School 181 believes that it is essential for our students to give back and therefore all children at our school are involved in supporting our community and making a difference in the lives of others. Students develop and lead an array of community service projects within the school, such as Toy Drives for young children in our community, Autism Awareness activities, fundraising for cancer research, and kindness campaigns. A dress code is in place at Middle School 181. Each grade level is assigned a specific polo shirt color to wear.","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":"5 to Baychester Av","bus":"Bx12, Bx12-SBS, Bx23, Bx25, Bx26, Bx28, Bx30, Bx38, BxM7, Q50","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Co-op City","latitude":40.875007,"longitude":-73.831749,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.955],"st":["ok"],"n":[329.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.932,0.946,0.944,0.911,0.918,0.919,0.919],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[915.0,904.0,861.0,780.0,675.0,591.0,521.0],"c":[null,null,null,null,null,1.0,0.899]},"attendance_remote_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.943],"st":["ok"],"n":[859.0]},"chronic_absent_ems_all":{"y":["2015-16","2016-17","2017-18","2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.788,0.809,0.793,0.764,0.849,0.825,0.698,0.718,0.697,0.68],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[879.0,870.0,897.0,908.0,888.0,856.0,761.0,662.0,581.0,509.0],"c":[0.836,0.796,0.783,0.771,null,null,null,0.696,0.904,0.724],"s":[3.0,2.5,2.83,2.85,null,null,null,3.01,4.83,1.1]},"chronic_absent_ems_allea":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.933,0.889,0.942,0.885,0.872,0.808,0.739],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[45.0,45.0,52.0,52.0,47.0,52.0,46.0],"c":[0.819,null,null,null,null,null,null]},"chronic_absent_ems_alleb":{"y":["2018-19","20